{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And the cloud of HaShem was upon them by day.</b> What Rashi explained — that seven clouds are mentioned in their journeys — they are not all written in one passage, as in Tanchuma: From here they said: there are seven clouds — 'and the cloud of HaShem was upon them by day' here; 'and Your cloud stood over them' — 'in a pillar of cloud You stand over them' and 'in a pillar of cloud You go before them by day' from the passage of Shelach; 'and when the cloud lingered' in this passage; 'and when the cloud lifted'; 'and if the cloud did not lift'; 'for the cloud of HaShem was upon the Mishkan' from the passage of Pekudei. Rabbi Yehudah says: there were thirteen — two for each direction, and two above, and two below, and one in front of them — the tall one lowered itself and the low one raised itself. Rabbi Yoshiyah says: four. Rabbi [Yehudah haNasi] says: two."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:19.454089504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}